
  Operate a cairn-cms production site.                                                                                  
                                                                                                                        
  To set up a new site, run `cairn new`. `cairn new --help` covers running it at a terminal and from an agent.          
  Run `cairn help agents` for the contract a program reads.                                                             
  Pass --json to a reporting command for a machine-readable payload on stdout.                                          
  Set CAIRN_PLAIN=1 to print plain output at a terminal, the same output a pipe receives.                               
  Exit codes: 0 OK, 1 WARNING, 2 CRITICAL, 3 UNKNOWN.                                                                   
         
  [1mUSAGE[m  
         
    cairn [command] [--flags]      
            
  [1mEXAMPLES[m  
            
    # Check a site's health        
    $ cairn health my-site-a1b2c3  
                                   
    # Set up a new site            
    $ cairn new                    
                  
  [1mSITE COMMANDS:[m  
                  
    adopt [command] [--flags]  Add a Cloudflare Worker to the registry as a site
    doctor [<dir>] [--flags]   Check a cairn-cms site's configuration, no credential or deploy needed
    health [<site>] [--flags]  Run the read-only health checks against one site, or every site when none is named
    logs <site> [--flags]      Read one site's engine log records
    new [command] [--flags]    Set up a new cairn site
    sites [command] [--flags]  List the sites cairn knows
                        
  [1mCREDENTIAL COMMANDS:[m  
                        
    auth [command]             Manage credentials in the OS keyring
                   
  [1mOTHER COMMANDS:[m  
                   
    agents                     Print the contract a program or an agent reads
    completion [command]       Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
    help [command]             Help about any command
         
  [1mFLAGS[m  
         
    --ack-file                 Path to a JSON file of holds (default: acknowledgements.json in the registry directory)
    --color                    When to colour the output: auto, always, or never (auto)
    -h --help                  Help for cairn
    -q --quiet                 Print nothing when the run is OK
    --theme                    The ground to render for: dark or light (dark)
    -t --timeout               Wall-Clock budget for the whole run (8m0s)
    -v --verbose               Print the identifiers a run otherwise withholds
    -V --version               Print the version and exit
    --width                    Columns to render at, instead of the terminal's width

